    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "Sample answer: $9,29,29,29$ years.\n\nThe total is $96$ years, giving a mean of $24$ years; the two middle ages are both $29$ years.",
      "worked": "Choose the two middle ages and the largest age to be $29$ years. The required total age is $4\\times24=96$ years.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Remaining age}&=96-3\\times29\\\\\\text{Remaining age}&=9\\text{ years}\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe ordered ages are $9,29,29,29$ years. Check:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Mean}&=\\frac{9+29+29+29}{4}\\\\\\text{Mean}&=24\\text{ years}\\\\\\text{Median}&=\\frac{29+29}{2}\\\\\\text{Median}&=29\\text{ years}\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
